01:42:03.510 --> 01:42:06.768
but there's plenty of professionals out there to say

2625
01:42:06.768 --> 01:42:08.090
"You know what this is all part of it.

2626
01:42:08.090 --> 01:42:09.240
This is what to expect."

2627
01:42:09.240 --> 01:42:11.510
But at least educating them on that.

2628
01:42:11.510 --> 01:42:14.080
Like this is out there, be ready for it.

2629
01:42:14.080 --> 01:42:15.930
And you think you might be prepared.

2630
01:42:15.930 --> 01:42:16.780
But when your mother

2631
01:42:16.780 --> 01:42:18.260
and mother-in-law finally leave

2632
01:42:18.260 --> 01:42:19.270
and you're alone in the house

2633
01:42:19.270 --> 01:42:21.780
and you can't sleep and you've totally look

2634
01:42:21.780 --> 01:42:23.500
at your body and you're not getting any training done

2635
01:42:23.500 --> 01:42:24.500
and you're like pooh

2636
01:42:25.850 --> 01:42:27.700
that's when things start going south.

2637
01:42:28.843 --> 01:42:30.020
And it's hard to prepare.

2638
01:42:30.020 --> 01:42:32.084
I mean, you can prepare people for these things

2639
01:42:32.084 --> 01:42:35.760
but everyone's experience is going to be different

2640
01:42:35.760 --> 01:42:37.760
through that transition, no matter what.

2641
01:42:37.760 --> 01:42:41.760
You just said with experience

2642
01:42:41.760 --> 01:42:43.820
and her going into those classrooms

2643
01:42:43.820 --> 01:42:46.350
I think the important thing there is too,

2644
01:42:46.350 --> 01:42:48.790
like you said, allowing ourselves to fail.

2645
01:42:48.790 --> 01:42:50.850
And a lot of good coaching

2646
01:42:50.850 --> 01:42:53.150
in my opinion is exactly that.

2647
01:42:53.150 --> 01:42:55.170
Allow setting the conditions

2648
01:42:55.170 --> 01:42:56.870
and environment for you to fail.

2649
01:42:56.870 --> 01:43:00.497
And having a guide, mentor, coach to say,

2650
01:43:00.497 --> 01:43:01.330
"You know what?

2651
01:43:01.330 --> 01:43:02.570
That was expected.

2652
01:43:02.570 --> 01:43:04.120
You should be here.

2653
01:43:04.120 --> 01:43:05.130
And that is awesome.

2654
01:43:05.130 --> 01:43:07.150
Now, what are we gonna do with it?"

2655
01:43:07.150 --> 01:43:10.700
How are you as an athlete learning to go forward from this

2656
01:43:10.700 --> 01:43:14.460
using what you just experienced with me, helping you

2657
01:43:14.460 --> 01:43:18.370
along the way, guiding you forward, failing forward.

2658
01:43:18.370 --> 01:43:21.330
So that then you're going to be a better, smarter, stronger

2659
01:43:21.330 --> 01:43:23.340
better athlete post this.

2660
01:43:23.340 --> 01:43:25.823
But you have to go through those failures.

2661
01:43:27.490 --> 01:43:30.610
It has to be a tactile experience for that individual.

2662
01:43:30.610 --> 01:43:34.530
You're performing as a coach, some form of inception

2663
01:43:34.530 --> 01:43:38.350
because you could just say, "Here's what you need to do.

2664
01:43:38.350 --> 01:43:39.570
Why aren't you doing this?"

2665
01:43:39.570 --> 01:43:44.260
But the letting go and the allowing allows that person

2666
01:43:44.260 --> 01:43:48.100
to then see where those edges are, whatever fail.

2667
01:43:48.100 --> 01:43:49.720
And then they can like take ownership

2668
01:43:49.720 --> 01:43:50.620
of it in a different way.

2669
01:43:50.620 --> 01:43:52.370
Like they get it in a way they wouldn't

2670
01:43:52.370 --> 01:43:55.733
if they were just trying to follow your lead all the time.

2671
01:43:55.733 --> 01:43:58.566
There's a theory out there that, you know

2672
01:43:58.566 --> 01:44:00.766
I think it was a quote by Bismarck who said,

2673
01:44:01.607 --> 01:44:03.430
"I don't wanna learn through experience.

2674
01:44:03.430 --> 01:44:05.500
I wanna learn through other people's experience

2675
01:44:05.500 --> 01:44:07.130
so I can avoid those mistakes."

2676
01:44:07.130 --> 01:44:09.260
No, in my opinion, no

2677
01:44:09.260 --> 01:44:12.280
because I am incorporating, I'm learning, I'm working in

2678
01:44:12.280 --> 01:44:15.460
and working out when I'm going through those failures

2679
01:44:15.460 --> 01:44:17.910
I'm able to analyze it, feel it mentally

2680
01:44:17.910 --> 01:44:21.030
physically, spiritually, completely different.

2681
01:44:21.030 --> 01:44:21.863
Going through that.

2682
01:44:21.863 --> 01:44:23.983
Because was Mark didn't have teenage daughters.

2683
01:44:25.940 --> 01:44:27.014
That's a good one.

2684
01:44:27.014 --> 01:44:29.210
Very true three of them.

2685
01:44:31.587 --> 01:44:33.250
I mean look, I'm a woman.

2686
01:44:33.250 --> 01:44:36.403
I can speak for that side of it 'cause it is very true.

2687
01:44:39.287 --> 01:44:42.833
I think there's like when you're saying,

2688
01:44:44.250 --> 01:44:48.870
he wants people to avoid these mistakes

2689
01:44:48.870 --> 01:44:50.790
before they go into it.

2690
01:44:50.790 --> 01:44:55.150
I get so frustrated when I hear people wanting advice

2691
01:44:55.150 --> 01:44:56.460
or telling me how to do this

2692
01:44:56.460 --> 01:44:59.060
or please tell me how to do this right now.

2693
01:44:59.060 --> 01:45:00.360
And it's something I'm working on

2694
01:45:00.360 --> 01:45:01.860
not getting frustrated with

2695
01:45:01.860 --> 01:45:04.190
but it is something that is difficult

2696
01:45:04.190 --> 01:45:07.830
because I just so badly want to just say

2697
01:45:07.830 --> 01:45:10.890
you have to learn this through your own experience

2698
01:45:10.890 --> 01:45:14.850
and take an integrate things that other people have said.

2699
01:45:14.850 --> 01:45:18.400
And showed you so that you can then integrate it

2700
01:45:18.400 --> 01:45:21.080
into your own body and your own experience.

2701
01:45:21.080 --> 01:45:23.790
It's like, you don't want to be the next Serena Williams.

2702
01:45:23.790 --> 01:45:28.320
You wanna be Coco like you wanna be your own athlete.

2703
01:45:28.320 --> 01:45:31.880
And I think that that is something I'm so passionate about.

2704
01:45:31.880 --> 01:45:33.280
And I get all the fields about that

2705
01:45:33.280 --> 01:45:37.440
because it's a powerful thing as we evolve in society.

2706
01:45:37.440 --> 01:45:39.280
And there's a lot of information out there.

2707
01:45:39.280 --> 01:45:40.700
And there's a lot of people telling you

2708
01:45:40.700 --> 01:45:41.700
how to do different things

2709
01:45:41.700 --> 01:45:43.330
and coaches telling you,

2710
01:45:43.330 --> 01:45:44.780
"Well this is the way to do it."

2711
01:45:44.780 --> 01:45:46.250
And it's like the ones that can walk

2712
01:45:46.250 --> 01:45:48.030
alongside you and allow you to fail forward

2713
01:45:48.030 --> 01:45:50.583
and allow you to make your own mistakes.

2714
01:45:52.080 --> 01:45:53.460
It frustrates people.

2715
01:45:53.460 --> 01:45:55.130
It's very frustrating for sure.

2716
01:45:55.130 --> 01:45:56.460
It's hard to be in that position.

2717
01:45:56.460 --> 01:45:59.650
Well, but it's also frustrating for the athlete.

2718
01:45:59.650 --> 01:46:01.010
I'm used to watching it now

2719
01:46:01.010 --> 01:46:03.670
because it's very predictable.

2720
01:46:03.670 --> 01:46:06.190
But A there's an industry out there

2721
01:46:06.190 --> 01:46:09.470
of coaches who will shortcut it with you.

2722
01:46:09.470 --> 01:46:10.490
That's my job.

2723
01:46:10.490 --> 01:46:13.300
You, hack the system by working with me.

2724
01:46:13.300 --> 01:46:15.780
I'll get you around those shortcuts.

2725
01:46:15.780 --> 01:46:17.270
Well A in the endurance world, we know

2726
01:46:17.270 --> 01:46:18.860
that especially doesn't work.

2727
01:46:18.860 --> 01:46:21.930
But B it's also the athlete

2728
01:46:21.930 --> 01:46:25.450
the person, the coachee thinks that

2729
01:46:25.450 --> 01:46:27.010
because they hired you.

2730
01:46:27.010 --> 01:46:30.120
They get to jump ahead in the line,

2731
01:46:30.120 --> 01:46:31.920
ahead in the path of life.

2732
01:46:31.920 --> 01:46:36.920
And it's like, no good coaching is mentorship.

2733
01:46:37.103 --> 01:46:39.967
Being a few steps ahead, maybe, and saying

2734
01:46:39.967 --> 01:46:44.720
"You know what, when you grab that branch, be careful."

2735
01:46:44.720 --> 01:46:46.110
You're still gonna grab the branch

2736
01:46:46.110 --> 01:46:49.910
as you're climbing the tree, but just heads up right now.

2737
01:46:49.910 --> 01:46:54.760
Or what I like to always do is imagine a good coach

2738
01:46:54.760 --> 01:46:56.880
is the guy who stands by or the girl who stands behind you

2739
01:46:56.880 --> 01:47:00.618
and just takes your shoulders and goes just this way.

2740
01:47:00.618 --> 01:47:01.451
Just a little bit.

2741
01:47:01.451 --> 01:47:04.427
You're still going your path, but just a little nudge here

2742
01:47:04.427 --> 01:47:06.910
and there so that you again are heading

2743
01:47:06.910 --> 01:47:09.060
with those buffers bumpers.

2744
01:47:09.060 --> 01:47:12.340
Setting the conditions to get to where you wanna go.

2745
01:47:12.340 --> 01:47:13.173
What kind of athlete were you?

2746
01:47:13.173 --> 01:47:14.695
Did you want the answers?

2747
01:47:14.695 --> 01:47:15.570
What did you like?

2748
01:47:15.570 --> 01:47:18.493
No, I was such a scared little kid.

2749
01:47:19.730 --> 01:47:22.420
And that's the funny thing is I had

2750
01:47:22.420 --> 01:47:24.570
I just talked about this, I think

2751
01:47:24.570 --> 01:47:27.130
on my podcast about how I never won anything.

2752
01:47:27.130 --> 01:47:29.020
I always had bigger, stronger athletes

2753
01:47:29.020 --> 01:47:30.500
around me that were just awesome.

2754
01:47:30.500 --> 01:47:33.260
They were just, six foot, two.

2755
01:47:33.260 --> 01:47:38.260
Big, I mean, in like middle school, like these icons

2756
01:47:38.420 --> 01:47:40.270
and I was always just the little kid.

2757
01:47:41.600 --> 01:47:43.350
I always felt never good enough

2758
01:47:43.350 --> 01:47:44.950
part of the tears back then too.

2759
01:47:44.950 --> 01:47:46.630
Like, it just was never good enough.

2760
01:47:46.630 --> 01:47:50.590
I was just always below the surface of feeling good enough.

2761
01:47:50.590 --> 01:47:53.020
And so I stood there with the puppy.

2762
01:47:53.020 --> 01:47:56.330
I did everything and oh, you want me to sleep more?

2763
01:47:56.330 --> 01:47:59.150
And then I tried everything.

2764
01:47:59.150 --> 01:48:01.510
So I was very compliant

2765
01:48:01.510 --> 01:48:04.040
but I also loved the structure and the discipline.

2766
01:48:04.040 --> 01:48:07.332
So I think I was coachable

2767
01:48:07.332 --> 01:48:09.800
