before society sort of-

2815
01:50:05.137 --> 01:50:05.970
Squeezed it out of them.

2816
01:50:05.970 --> 01:50:07.685
You must be like this.

2817
01:50:07.685 --> 01:50:09.333
Which is why it's like,

2818
01:50:10.210 --> 01:50:11.380
if you're gonna grab that branch

2819
01:50:11.380 --> 01:50:13.230
you might want to think about that.

2820
01:50:13.230 --> 01:50:15.190
When you were telling that story,

2821
01:50:15.190 --> 01:50:18.703
it reminds me of like sponsorship in AA.

2822
01:50:19.720 --> 01:50:20.850
Doing this for many years.

2823
01:50:20.850 --> 01:50:23.450
And it's like, you get crazy calls.

2824
01:50:23.450 --> 01:50:24.960
And people are like, "Well

2825
01:50:24.960 --> 01:50:26.520
maybe you need to go out and drink some more."

2826
01:50:26.520 --> 01:50:29.160
And they're like "Let me know how that goes.

2827
01:50:29.160 --> 01:50:30.600
Call me next week."

2828
01:50:30.600 --> 01:50:33.130
It's like I'm not telling you not to do,

2829
01:50:33.130 --> 01:50:35.530
well it sounds like you really want to drink.

2830
01:50:35.530 --> 01:50:36.490
So maybe you should.

2831
01:50:36.490 --> 01:50:37.323
Allowing them-

2832
01:50:37.323 --> 01:50:40.360
They have to like make that decision for themselves.

2833
01:50:40.360 --> 01:50:41.482
For sure.

2834
01:50:41.482 --> 01:50:43.690
I appreciate coaches like that though.

2835
01:50:43.690 --> 01:50:44.540
I really do.

2836
01:50:44.540 --> 01:50:47.660
That allow you to, like you were saying, fail forward

2837
01:50:47.660 --> 01:50:48.717
make the decisions for yourself.

2838
01:50:48.717 --> 01:50:52.060
And I think I was more of the John Moffitt type myself.

2839
01:50:52.060 --> 01:50:53.300
So I can only speak to that.

2840
01:50:53.300 --> 01:50:54.960
But my brother's the exact opposite.

2841
01:50:54.960 --> 01:50:57.070
He's very much play by the rules.

2842
01:50:57.070 --> 01:50:59.970
So I grew up very close in age to somebody

2843
01:50:59.970 --> 01:51:00.927
that was exact opposite of me.

2844
01:51:00.927 --> 01:51:04.030
And so it is interesting to have that experience

2845
01:51:04.030 --> 01:51:07.770
as I reflect back now on coaching and what that looks

2846
01:51:07.770 --> 01:51:11.250
like growing up and how that can evolve and change.

2847
01:51:11.250 --> 01:51:13.860
And how the athlete can also evolve and change.

2848
01:51:13.860 --> 01:51:15.847
If they are someone that is a rule follower and this

2849
01:51:15.847 --> 01:51:17.860
and this, they can use that to their advantage

2850
01:51:17.860 --> 01:51:20.450
if they choose to, to become great.

2851
01:51:20.450 --> 01:51:22.570
That can actually play into their advantage

2852
01:51:22.570 --> 01:51:25.870
in a way that I wouldn't understand.

2853
01:51:25.870 --> 01:51:27.430
I wouldn't be able to begin to understand.

2854
01:51:27.430 --> 01:51:29.633
But there's a lot of that going on.

2855
01:51:32.600 --> 01:51:34.610
You have the athletes like John, where it's like-

2856
01:51:34.610 --> 01:51:36.210
When that comes out in you though,

2857
01:51:36.210 --> 01:51:37.653
like what you're talking about

2858
01:51:37.653 --> 01:51:40.380
like either end of the spectrum, the rule follower

2859
01:51:40.380 --> 01:51:43.600
or the more creative again, once you're connected

2860
01:51:43.600 --> 01:51:47.570
